.TH LUFTLIFT 1 "October 2026" "opendrop-rs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luftlift \- AirDrop application protocol client and receiver for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luftlift
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luftlift
implements AirDrop discovery, HTTPS/TLS transfer, and dvzip/CPIO payload
handling. It normally runs over the
.B awdl0
interface created by
.BR filin ,
but discovery can also be used on another IPv6-capable interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -i ", --interface " interface
Network interface to use. The default is awdl0.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B receive
Advertise an AirDrop receiver and save incoming files.
.TP
.B find
Browse for AirDrop peers.
.TP
.B send
Send a file to a discovered AirDrop receiver.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
luftlift -i awdl0 find -d 5
luftlift -i awdl0 receive -o ./incoming
luftlift -i awdl0 send RECIPIENT photo.jpg
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LUFTLIFT_NAME
Base receiver name advertised through AirDrop.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter used for diagnostic logging.
.SH NOTES
Sending to an idle Apple device may require a Bluetooth LE wake-up
advertisement that this version of opendrop-rs does not provide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR filin (1)
